[{:db/id "q-89877/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0fab083c-880e-5970-975a-d44019d64402" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89877/selection/9e11fca0829731bcf7095fbe08d3f9c3c971cefec622b1eff73bc972ba625ef6" :answer/id #uuid "6aa8e7e2-e5e2-5858-be5e-822390946ed7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89877/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d" :answer/id #uuid "c5df7c42-2476-5c73-b111-e2ae40cd4523" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89877/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "00318461-d584-5b79-8cb2-d4db81436019" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89877/selection/de2f9e8d93e24093f903d192e87652a275278440944fbfbf925ef2d61e21dc26" :answer/id #uuid "8fb095b5-1f19-53e0-9c80-f68032971793" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89877/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "40d1ca0f-9023-5861-a019-e6a4b20f6814" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89877/selection/9e11fca0829731bcf7095fbe08d3f9c3c971cefec622b1eff73bc972ba625ef6" :answer-field/choices ["q-89877/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-89877/selection/9e11fca0829731bcf7095fbe08d3f9c3c971cefec622b1eff73bc972ba625ef6" "q-89877/selection/a2301b8122c312044fb5dc0b0c60c599b4f2f7f4ffcc198c9893873ab9165c9d" "q-89877/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-89877/selection/de2f9e8d93e24093f903d192e87652a275278440944fbfbf925ef2d61e21dc26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89877" :question/id #uuid "53528337-03e6-5063-9c35-a289ac5e1733" :question/math-academy-id "q-89877" :question/problem "The function $y=f(x)$ satisfies the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nGiven that the point $P(-1,0)$ lies on the graph of the function, evaluate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "To find an expression for the second derivative, we differentiate the equation with respect to $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y+{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the given expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ into the above and simplify the resulting expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =(y+{e}^{x})+{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =y+2{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the coordinates of our point into the above expression for the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}|}_{(-1,0)} & ={(y+2{e}^{x})|}_{(-1,0)} \\\\  & =0+2{e}^{-1} \\\\  & =2{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-89877/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f28fbcc-6d9c-5dc7-89cc-13255db78765"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89877"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-89886/selection/5b9c802d18c696e381de34b079b23666e71382895bc76576ccd26b9e32c10117" :answer/id #uuid "0e86a70c-2ef9-549d-b428-2dbd8d5279b7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89886/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "94fbe1e3-180d-59a4-a78b-8b4b296aa5bf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89886/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "0af3adb6-1511-568e-9518-6bf634e085b7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89886/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "c25a3ebb-d712-51a0-9ef7-0173c50102ba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89886/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "eabe37c3-ef66-56f9-b19b-a528f37c140a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89886/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b3fcb6d6-38d4-592e-977d-eb0c4153e39c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89886/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-89886/selection/5b9c802d18c696e381de34b079b23666e71382895bc76576ccd26b9e32c10117" "q-89886/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-89886/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-89886/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-89886/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89886" :question/id #uuid "9bddc166-b2f0-55f1-a976-9d329862898d" :question/math-academy-id "q-89886" :question/problem "The function $y=f(x)$ satisfies the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y-x.\n$$\n\nGiven that the point $(0,0)$ lies on the graph of $y=f(x),$ which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $(0,0)$ is a stationary point of the function $f$\n- $(0,0)$ is a local minimum point of the function $f$\n- $(0,0)$ is an inflection point of the function $f$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the value of the first and second derivatives of the function at the given point.\n\nTo find the first derivative of $f$ at $(0,0),$ we substitute the coordinates of our point into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,0)} & ={(y-x)|}_{(0,0)} \\\\  & =0-0 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the second derivative, we first need to differentiate the equation and then substitute the coordinates of the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y-x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-1 \\\\  & =(y-x)-1 \\\\  & =y-x-1 \\\\ {\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}|}_{(0,0)} & ={(y-x-1)|}_{(0,0)} \\\\  & =0-0-1 \\\\  & =-1 \\\\  & <0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since\n\n$$\n{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(0,0)}=0,\n$$\n\nwe obtain that $(0,0)$ is a stationary point of the function $f.$\n\n- Statement II is false. There is a critical point at $(0,0).$ So, according to the second derivative test, since\n\n$$\n{\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}|}_{(0,0)}<0,\n$$\n\nwe have a local maximum (not a local minimum) at that point.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the second derivative is not zero, there is no inflection point at $(0,0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-89886/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f901a3ab-3b58-51a1-b653-f88ac4b09060"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89886"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
